<title>UK: British Energy March output dips.</title>
<headline>British Energy March output dips.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nuclear electricity producer British Energy said on Friday that total sales reached 5.25 Twh in March 1997, down from 5.63 Twh a year ago.</p>
<p>A Terrawatt hour is the largest unit of measurement for electricity sales, representing one billion kilowatt hours.</p>
<p>The following table details sales from each power station in Twh:</p>
<p>	   1997		   1996</p>
<p>Station   March/Yr to date   March/Yr to date</p>
<p>Hinkley Pt B  0.82  8.14     0.86   9.99</p>
<p>Hunterston B  0.79  8.03     0.79   8.71</p>
<p>Dungeness B   0.18  6.68     0.42   2.39</p>
<p>Heysham 1     0.70  8.19     0.43   6.28</p>
<p>Hartlepool    0.44  8.63     0.62   7.38</p>
<p>Torness	 0.91  9.65     0.78   8.91</p>
<p>Heysham 2     0.53  9.44     0.86   9.65</p>
<p>Sizewell B    0.88  8.45     0.87   7.94</p>
<p>TOTAL SALES   5.25  67.21    5.63   61.25</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
